The heart of the matter:<p><pre><code>  struct Q&lt;T: &#x27;static&gt;(Option&lt;T&gt;);

  impl&lt;T: &#x27;static&gt; Drop for Q&lt;T&gt; {
    fn drop(&amp;mut self) {
        &#x2F;&#x2F; Code in here has access to a non-&#x27;static &amp;String
        &#x2F;&#x2F; but assumes that it&#x27;s a &amp;&#x27;static String
    }
  }

  fn main() {
    let l = String::new();
    let mut q = Q(None);
    q.0 = Some(&amp;l);
  }
</code></pre>
I wonder if the certified compiler for safety critical uses has the same issue.
